# x86Code configuration: copy to x86sim.env (gitignored) and adjust. Plain sh assignments; $X86SIM_ROOT is the
# repo root. Environment variables of the same name override this file. Never put the sudo password here: export
# SUDO_PASS in the shell that needs it (Darling install, killing setuid launchers, cores) or use a cached sudo.

# Darling install prefix (cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=...; bin/darling must be setuid root)
X86SIM_PREFIX=$X86SIM_ROOT/darling-prefix
# RuntimeRoot of the iOS 27.2 (24B8117) arm64 simulator runtime (x86sim runtime fetch 24B8117)
X86SIM_RUNTIME=$X86SIM_ROOT/runtimes/ios-27.2-24B8117-arm64/RuntimeRoot
# Darling build directory (cmake -B; make darling configures it)
#X86SIM_DARLING_BUILD=$X86SIM_ROOT/external/darling/build
# the default phone for CLI commands that take none (x86sim device create / the launcher make others; its data/ is the
# phone's home). Its UDID is derived from this path, so keep it stable once the phone has booted.
X86SIM_DEVICE=$X86SIM_ROOT/var/device-a64
# sockets, pid files and logs of a boot (mtlvk.sock, mDNSResponder, boot.log, ...)
X86SIM_STATE=$X86SIM_ROOT/var/run
# large scratch files: cores, maps, the progress site (never /tmp if it is a small tmpfs)
X86SIM_SCRATCH=$HOME/scratch/x86code
# Mac with Xcode for build/mac-build-*.sh (ssh, BatchMode), e.g. user@my-mac.local
X86SIM_MAC=
# progress site (x86sim site): served directory and local port of its http server / tunnel
X86SIM_SITE=$X86SIM_SCRATCH/site
X86SIM_SITE_PORT=8765

# GPU (Metal stand-in on Vulkan): X86CODE_METAL=all (default: every process), 0 (software rendering) or a
# comma-separated process list. mtlvk picks the first Vulkan device; to choose one use the Vulkan loader /
# Mesa variables, e.g. VK_ICD_FILENAMES=/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/nvidia_icd.json or MESA_VK_DEVICE_SELECT=1002:73bf
#X86CODE_METAL=all
#VK_ICD_FILENAMES=
#MESA_VK_DEVICE_SELECT=
# mtlvk binary (make mtlvk)
#X86SIM_MTLVK=$X86SIM_ROOT/linux/mtlvk/target/release/mtlvk


# Disk guard: a phone runs in a systemd user scope capped at X86SIM_IO_MAX bytes/s of reads and writes (default 40M;
# 0 = no scope) and X86SIM_IO_IOPS reads/s (default 4000), with low IO/CPU weight (X86SIM_CPU_WEIGHT, default 40).
#X86SIM_IO_MAX=40M
